----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SIGNOFF PERSON EXTRACTION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Extract one object per signoff person. If multiple people signed, create separate objects for each.

A "signoff person" is defined as an individual who has a dedicated execution block intended for a signature. 

CRITICAL EXCLUSION: Do NOT extract individuals from tabular lists, signature specimen schedules, or authorization rosters (e.g., lists of "Authorized Signatories" or "Local Signatories" in an Exhibit or Annex) unless they also have a primary execution block at the end of the main document text.

FIELDS TO EXTRACT:

1. NAME
   Extract the full printed name of each person in the signature block. 
   Source: Look below or adjacent to the physical signature line.

2. DESIGNATION
   Extract the role/title of the signoff person.
   Source: Look directly below or next to the printed name. 
   Note: If the title is bilingual or multi-lingual (e.g., "Vorstandsvorsitzender / Chairman of the Board of Management"), extract the entire string exactly as written. 
   If no title is present in the signature block, scan the document's introductory preamble to infer their capacity (e.g., "Director"). If it cannot be determined anywhere, set "NA".

OUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE:

{
  "Signoff_Persons": [
    {
      "Name": "Ola Källenius",
      "Designation": "Vorstandsvorsitzender / Chairman of the Board of Management"
    },
    {
      "Name": "Harald Wilhelm",
      "Designation": "Finanzvorstand / Chief Financial Officer"
    }
  ]
}
